WHAT THIS COVERS
----------------

The study content in this directory, which is original work written for this
project:

  questions/            386 original exam-style questions, with the rationale
                        for the key and for every distractor
  cases/                branching audit scenarios
  study-guides/         one guide per domain
  principles.json       the decision-rule taxonomy
  confusable-pairs.json documented confusions and their discriminators

The software in the rest of the repository is MIT licensed - see ../LICENSE.
Where the two meet, the rule is simple: the engine is MIT, the material it
reads is CC BY-SA.

WHAT THIS DOES NOT COVER
------------------------

`outline.json` is a structural transcription of ISACA's published CISA exam
content outline - domain names, section names, topic names and the published
domain weights. That is ISACA's material and their trademark, and no licence
is claimed over it here. It is included because the tool needs the topic
vocabulary to tag questions against, and it is facts and headings rather than
prose. Verify it against isaca.org rather than trusting this copy.

Nothing in this directory is reproduced or adapted from ISACA's official
materials, the QAE database, or any other exam bank. Every question is
original.

